# Linear completion notes (all repos)

When you mark a Linear issue **Done** (or otherwise complete it) in any site or repo, **append** a completion comment on that issue before ending the turn. Do this for every completed ticket, including follow-ups you close in the same session.

## How

- Use the Linear workspace that owns the issue (`save_comment` with `issueId` + `body`).
- **Append only.** Do not rewrite or replace the original description, acceptance criteria, or earlier comments.
- If the issue was completed by someone else and has no completion note, add one when you are the one closing it.

## What to include

A short Markdown comment titled `Completed` covering only what actually shipped to finish **this** ticket:

- What changed (behavior, not a file dump)
- Where (repo, key paths, PR/commit SHA if one exists)
- How it was verified
- Deploy or release state if this ticket required one (`shipped` / `not deployed`)
- Anything explicitly left out of scope

Skip secrets, credentials, and PII. One comment per completed issue; do not batch several tickets into one note.
